<div class="needs"><span><strong>Download:</strong> <a href="../../code/talk-reveal.js.zip">talk-reveal.js.zip</a>, the presentation and its models (<code>demos/</code>), ready to show (see its <code>README.md</code>).</span><span><strong>Show it:</strong> <code>python3 -m http.server 8080</code> in its folder, then <code>http://localhost:8080/</code></span></div>

One HTML file holds the whole presentation, a `<section>` per slide. The models are in `demos/` next to it:

```
talk-reveal/
  README.md              how to show it
  index.html             the presentation, below
  demos/
    a1/ a2/ c3/ c6/ c7/  the web builds of the examples: index.html, project.js, project.wasm, project.data
    slide-controls.js    the buttons of the slides
```

- A slide with a model: a `<div class="side">` with the text on the left and the frame on the right.
- `data-src` loads a model when its slide comes near, and unloads it after: the models of the other slides
  do not run.
- All the slides are in one page: the buttons of a slide name their model (`data-demo="#surface"`).

