</div>

<div class="needs"><span><strong>Download:</strong> <a href="../../code/talk-lhtml-site.zip">talk-lhtml-site.zip</a>, the sources of the presentation and its models (<code>src/_demo/</code>)</span><span><strong>Build it:</strong> <code>lhtml-site</code> in its folder, then <code>lhtml-site --serve</code></span></div>

A folder per slide, in the order of their names. The models are in `src/_demo/`; a folder whose name starts
with an underscore is not a slide, it is copied as it is.

```
talk-lhtml-site/
  README.md                    how to build and show it
  configure.yaml               the build: the slides in the browser, and a PDF
  src/
    01_title/index.html.j2     a slide: its title (=), its text, its model (demo::)
    02_outline/index.html.j2
    ...
    12_conclusion/index.html.j2
    _style/talk.css            the buttons of the slides, and the image of a model in the PDF
    _demo/a1/ ... _demo/c7/    the web builds of the examples, with their poster
    _demo/slide-controls.js
```

- A slide with a model: the layout `side` puts the text on the left and the `media::` block on the right.
- `demo::` writes the frame; `img::` gives the image of the model in the PDF (the classes `.live` and `.still`,
  and `_style/talk.css`).
- A slide shows one page: the buttons of a slide drive its model without naming it.
- `configure.yaml` loads the stylesheet and `slide-controls.js` in every slide (`cssAbs`, `jsAbs`).

